  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>About: AePS 4-way reconciliation. NPCI settlement master (driving side) is LEFT-joined on RRN to the UIDAI&#xd;&#xa;Aadhaar auth gateway, the BC micro-ATM terminal journal and the BC agent float GL-9904.&#xd;&#xa;STP rule: STATUS=SUCCESS and AUTH_STATUS=SUCCESS and DISPENSE_STATUS=DISPENSED and GL_STATUS=POSTED and zero GL variance.&#xd;&#xa;Exceptions: TERMINAL_TIMEOUT_91 / _96, DISPENSE_FAILURE, BIOMETRIC_MISMATCH, BIOMETRIC_SPOOF_ALERT (UIDAI 998),&#xd;&#xa;GL_FLOAT_VARIANCE, GL_NOT_POSTED, BC_AGENT_MISMATCH, MISSING_IN_UIDAI / TERMINAL / GL, STATUS_MISMATCH.&#xd;&#xa;Txn date / age is decoded from the RRN (YDDDHHnnnnnn) for the RBI T+1 TAT check downstream.&#xd;&#xa;&#xd;&#xa;Params: INPUT_DIR, OUTPUT_DIR (config), CYCLE_ID (runtime).&#xd;&#xa;Output: Matched_AePS_Records_&lt;yyyyMMdd_HHmmss&gt;.xlsx and Unmatched_AePS_Records_&lt;yyyyMMdd_HHmmss&gt;.xlsx; both paths are&#xd;&#xa;returned as o_matched_file / o_unmatched_file and attached to the workflow result.&#xd;&#xa;&#xd;&#xa;Errors: feeds are pre-validated (exists and non-empty) - a missing feed ends in Failure with the feed names.&#xd;&#xa;Malformed CSV rows go down per-feed error hops to the error log (their RRN surfaces as a MISSING_IN_x exception).</note>
      <xloc>64</xloc>
      <yloc>760</yloc>
      <width>900</width>
      <heigth>300</heigth>
      <fontname>Segoe UI</fontname>
      <fontsize>11</fontsize>
      <fontbold>N</fontbold>
      <fontitalic>N</fontitalic>
